 the outside says that if ishiki did  take kauki they're out of options  they're completely done for not a very  reassuring conclusion from our scientist  here however the hope is that naruto's  baryon mode  was enough to make sure that ishiki dies  before he succeeds and implanting his  karma into kawaki again  ishiki proceeds to count his chickens  before they hatch and assumes it's over  he won already in his mind but still he  acknowledges that it was a close call  and he only has five minutes left kawaki  recalls what amato said that even a  monster  can't escape death and instead of giving  up he focuses on trying to last for five  minutes so they can win  kind of not too smart of ishiki to  reveal how much time he has left and  kawaki is cocky too  saying stuff like he's glad ishiki  brought him here so he can witness the  end of his worthless life  talking to an otsutuki like that who  believe that they are infinitely  superior to humans  is great to see remember ishiki's goal  here is just to implant the karma and  then he can totally die no problem yeah  he won't resurrect right away but he  will eventually when the karma matures  naruto tells kawaki to run but he  doesn't have as much energy left as  ishiki ishiki delivers a blow to naruto  and he loses his baryon mode  this to me is kind of a good sign he  reverted back to normal and he's still  alive  again we don't know what the full  repercussions of using baryon mode  are going to be we just know that kurama  thought it would mean death  just as it all seems to be over and  ishiki is holding kaaki by the throat  sasuke uses his powers to switch places  with kawaki again i love how everyone is  playing their part here  sasuke gave kabuki some important  distance and also some smoke grenades  that are immune to the byakugan's powers  although sasuke is physically powerless  against ishiki and gets punched to the  ground  his strategy was great and very useful  here i love how he had left those smoke  grenades there on his feet before  switching places  the smoke only lasts a few minutes but  that's all they need  so mission seemingly accomplished but  and you know there's going to be a but  as we know villains don't give up that  easily and ishiki decides to use  naruto as a hostage he starts beating up  naruto so bad  kawaki's arm falls off showing that  naruto is seriously not in a good  position right now ishiki then gives  kawaki  20 seconds to show up or he'll kill  naruto when he only has a few minutes  left to live i wonder why he didn't give  like 10 seconds or something but  whatever the reason he gives 20 valuable  seconds in a situation where every  second counts we get a powerful  flashback of kawaki hiding from jigen  only to be found out  then jigen prepares to punish him with  his pull from the flashback it's implied  that this happened many times  so we can well assume that kawaki is  traumatized naruto's childhood was hard  and lonely there's no doubt about that  but kawaki was also punished mercilessly  and was trapped rather than allowed to  roam free that's why it's all the more  touching and powerful when after  remembering the kindness naruto showed  him  kawaki decides to give himself over with  less than a second left by the way bonus  points for kawaki  who made the most of the situation by  fully using those 20 important seconds  he uses fire release showing the fruits  of his ninjutsu training with naruto who  actually said that kawaki has a knack  for it but it seems to be no use  ishiki has caught him he insults him for  trying to be a ninja and trying to be  anything for that matter  he tells him he has no future besides  being sacrificed as ishiki's vessel and  we get some very powerful moments here  from kawaki again  making me respect him a lot i think  kawaki probably shines the most in this  entire chapter out of everyone he says  he was  empty but naruto gave him a reason to  live and in this time we live in where a  lot of people are especially in need of  a sense of meaning in their lives  a line like that hits home there's a  difference between simply existing and  truly living and naruto helped kalaki  realize that  then ishiki mentions the title of this  chapter when he says  who cares that naruto gave you a reason  to live when the reality of the  situation is  that kawaki was captured because of the  arm naruto gave him  and because of the affection he gave him  kawaki gave himself up  kawaki simply says that ishiki doesn't  understand a thing  and that a world without naruto has no  worth to him  kawaki would rather die than lose naruto  i'm sure if you asked kawaki if his life  before naruto was better than death he  would have said  no so even if he dies now he's still  super grateful that naruto took him out  of that deathlike meaningless existence  if only for a short period of time  and kawaki's actions here are really  brave and really honorable it really  makes me wonder how someone with so much  honor and such a strong moral compass  could end up being the kawaki we see  after the time skip in naruto we are  often introduced to a bad guy who  becomes a good guy  but here it seems that kawaki who's  willing to sacrifice his  own life for naruto right now will  actually end up being  boruto's main adversary it's crazy to  think about but right now i can't help  but be moved by kawaki's behavior and  actions  ishiki really doesn't care about any of  this emotional and honorable stuff  though he's like whatever the point is  you're just a vessel for me  he laughs like the joker as things seem  like they're all over the karma is back  on kawaki  however kishimoto is not done with the  twists  as it turns out kawaki's training in  ninjutsu was invaluable because it  taught him how to create shadow clones  and just when ishiki is about to die  happily with his mission accomplished  kabuki erases the karma marks on his  body ishiki is freaking out like never  before now and that's when the real  kawaki appears  and reveals that the other one is a  shadow clone love the use of strategy in  this chapter from sasuke's smoke  grenades and kawaki's shadow clone and i  also love the fact that everybody played  a crucial role  in buying time so they could finally win  and you gotta love how kawaki rubs it in  saying to ishiki who views them as lower  life forms or insect that he's gonna die  because he was totally outsmarted and  beaten by a mere vessel  and in fact this is his reality what an  amazing moment this  is although it leaves me wondering how  is kawaki going to get his karma  which we know he will get eventually but  on to the thing  we've been dying to know sasuke is beat  up for sure but he's curious about  naruto and the baryon mode  both kawaki and he along with us want  naruto to let them know  about the serious risk to that power and  what the consequences will be  but before naruto can explain boruto  possessed by momoshiki  stabs sasuke's renagon this means that  sasuke might have just lost his ability  to shift spaces  create portals to other dimensions and  more possibly forever  and it makes sense that momoshiki would  go for it since the rinnegan's powers  did annoy ishiki  a lot this is a huge loss and tragedy  for  sasuke especially after he was already  useless against ishiki's power  compared to naruto's baryon mode so we  are close to the end of this chapter and  now we have the situation with naruto  and the consequences of the baryon mode  being unclear  sasuke's rinagon potentially being  unusable forever and boruto taken over  by momoshiki  who would have thought that things would  look this bad  after they finally managed to defeat  ishiki momoshiki says he never thought  they would actually defeat ishiki but  he's glad because now they are the only  nuisances left  we don't know what he'll do whether  he'll go for the kill or if he'll leave  them in another dimension or what but  things do not look good  what a cliffhanger this is kishimoto is  really trying to make every chapter  count right now and i can't wait to see  where we go from here especially since  the stakes are so high and we got so  many  unanswered questions and that is it for  this video as always let me know your  thoughts on the chapter and what you  expect to see happening next in the  comments  if you do enjoy seeing naruto and boruto  videos on this channel and want to keep  them coming then the best thing you can  do is smash that like button and share  this video if you haven't be sure to  subscribe and this is crucial hit that  notification bell and select all or you  will miss  future naruto such porto videos so if  you haven't yet  make this the day you subscribe and as  you wait for the next boruto chapter or  video to drop  feel free to check out my growing naruto  playlist where i got videos about the  hokage  dotsutsuki the ozumaki and most recently  all 27 kage and their powers explained  which is actually  our longest naruto video on the channel  so make sure to check that out a lot of  interesting information there  links to the playlist and to the new  kanye video can be found  in the description and until next time  see ya space cowboys  [Music]  you

